// WQL — UNARY `-` HAS NO ENTRY IN THE UNSIGNED TOWER, AND THE REFUSAL SAYS SO
// RATHER THAN FALLING BACK TO THE SIGNED ONE.
//
// The EL's five unsigned operations are `el_addu`/`el_subu`/`el_mulu`/`el_divu`/
// `el_remu`. There is no `el_negu` and there will not be one: negation is not an
// operation on an unsigned value — every non-zero u64 has no image in the type.
// The signed tower's `el_neg` exists, and reaching it would mean reading the
// column as i64, which is the silent choice of signedness this whole seam
// refuses to make (`wql_arith_mixed_tower_fail` refuses the binary case).
//
// ⚠ A `u32` COLUMN IS NOT REFUSED HERE AND MUST NOT BE. `-s.w` over `u32` is
// admitted and answered (`wql_arith_narrow_e2e` claim 5): u32's tower IS the i64
// one, because every u32 value survives `as i64`, so `el_neg` is the node's own
// operation and not a substitution. The refusal is about the TOWER, not about
// the word "unsigned" — which is exactly the distinction a name list would lose.
package test;

use logos.std.wql.wql;
use logos.mem.collections.vec;

struct Rec { pub id: i64, pub u: u64 }

pub deem negd(src: &[Rec]) { from src s select -s.u }

fn main() -> i32 { return 0i32; }
